Following criteria are considered for awarding degrees,
a) Following the programme in the specified field of study for the minimum
stipulated period of time;
b) Satisfactory completion of the academic requirements of all semesters of the
Degree Programme;
c) As stipulated in the respective Degree Programme Curriculum obtaining a
minimum of GPA credits and a minimum of NGPA credits
d) Fulfilment of the criteria for completing the examinations within the maximum
stipulated time period;
e) Earning a GPA of not less than 2.00 for the entire degree programme;
f) Not having more than 1 D+ or C- grades per semester in the entire programme.
A student shall be entitled to the award of the Hons Degree unless he/she has completed
the above requirements (a – f) within four academic years.
